<title>ITALY: Italy's Naples sees Jan CPI at 0.4 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Naples sees Jan CPI at 0.4 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>NAPLES, Italy 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Naples said its January consumer price index stood at 0.4 percent month on month and 3.1 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In December, Naples' inflation rate was 0.2 percent and 3.0 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Naples is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.64 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.</p>
<p>Transmission was aborted</p>
<p>Transmission was aborted  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes:</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to December 1996)</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		   0.4 (0.2)	  3.1  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Food				0.2 (0.3)	  3.8  (3.8)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	 0.0 (0.2)	  2.1  (1.9)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges 1.4 (0.2)	  2.4  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Furniture			 0.0 (0.1)	  1.6  (0.8)</p>
<p>    Health services		 2.8 (0.0)	  2.4  (1.4)</p>
<p>    Transportation		  0.3 (0.0)	  5.1  (6.3)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture   0.0 (0.2)	  4.3  (4.2)</p>
<p>    Education			 0.0 (0.0)	  3.4  (1.7)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	0.0 (0.1)	  3.3  (3.2)</p>
<p>    Other goods and services    0.0 (0.1)	  1.9  (1.7)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
